  ],
  "text": "A blue whale's heart is about the size of a small car. Its tongue alone weighs roughly as much as an elephant. Thirty metres long. A hundred and fifty tonnes. A calf drinks enough milk to put on ninety kilos a day. Nothing on land ever came close. Not one dinosaur. Because on land it would not work at all. Its own weight would crush it. In water none of that weight sits on the bones. The sea carries all of it. The largest animal in history only exists because it never has to stand up. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
